From fd434fe8c603c5be3f0687b3f20fecf3dc405ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGbot <ggbot@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:48:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] v3.2 night sea: tint the live sea uniform (lazy,
 verified), journey tint #4a6a8c

Mac review of 764dcd8: the v3.1 tint never reached the pixels. The v3.1 binder ran once at prop load, read mainColor
with getProperty() as a byte Color and only adopted an existing RoomLightingRig instance; any miss left it off for good.
SeaNightTint reads/writes the pass uniform (linear Vec4, the API the verified WorldFlowComponent bindings use), re-binds
every tick until it holds the renderer's current material (and after a swap), takes its own instance after 2 s if nobody
instanced the sea, verifies each write by readback, and runs every sync (not only with the exterior layer).
Journey tint #4a6a8c: predicted night-journey sea Y 0.16-0.19 from the measured Mac pixels (target <= 0.25).
Day = authored uniform exactly. New test tools/t9-island-props/test_sea_night_tint.cjs (S1-S6).
